    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαπο-δύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strip</i> one <i>for combat against</i> another,
				<i>set</i> him <i>up as a rival to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.788d
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>strip and set to work at</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ πράγματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					615
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυοινίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.360
				</span></i>
			; <i>set upon, attack,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς νενικηκόσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Marc.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
